# Content ↔ footer / challenge gap

## Project detail (`/projects/[slug]`)

**bring me your challenge** sits **above Related** (`.project-detail__challenge`), not in the site footer.

- Challenge **top** pad = `90%` of `--challenge-band-pad-y` (GIF optical trim).
- Challenge **bottom** pad = `--related-rule-gap` — same as Related `padding-top` (line → “Related” title), so challenge → rule → title reads even.
- Token: `--related-rule-gap: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem)` on `.project-detail`.

## Site footer (all pages)

No challenge CTA. `.site-footer__gap` uses height `var(--content-footer-gap)` between page content and the black footer stage.

Black shell top pad: `--footer-top-gap` = **2×** the prior clamp (`calc(clamp(3.25rem, 5.75vw, 4.5rem) * 2)`).

## Tokens (`:root` in `app/globals.css`)

- `--challenge-band-pad-y` — **5.625rem (90px)** mobile; **7.5rem (120px)** from `900px` up
- `--content-footer-gap: var(--challenge-band-pad-y)`
- `--footer-top-gap` — black shell inner top pad (`.site-footer__shell`), doubled vs prior

## Do not

- Put “bring me your challenge” in the site footer or on non–project-detail pages
- Reintroduce `main` `padding-bottom` for footer air
- Stack Related `margin-top` on top of the challenge bottom pad
- Let challenge bottom pad diverge from `--related-rule-gap` / Related `padding-top`
